### Option 2: Convert the Exact Image Pixels into an Exportable 3D File (`.ply` / `.glb` / `.blend`)

If you need an exported 3D asset built directly from the exact pixels of your photograph for **Blender, Unreal Engine 5, or Unity**, use one of these single-image-to-3D AI pipelines:

1. **Single-Image 3D Gaussian Splatting (Best for Photorealistic Parallax & Foliage)**
   * **Apple `ml-sharp` (Open Source)** or **World Labs Marble**: Upload your bamboo image to generate a dense **3D Gaussian Splat (`.ply` / `.splat`)** in seconds. Unlike polygon meshes, Gaussian Splats preserve razor-sharp backlit leaves and thin overlapping bamboo stalks without jagged edges.
2. **Depth-to-Mesh Projection in Blender (Best for Camera Fly-Throughs)**
   * Run your photo through **Depth Anything V2** (free on Hugging Face Spaces) to generate a 16-bit depth map.
   * In **Blender**, align the wide-angle upward perspective with **fSpy**, project your photo onto a subdivided dome/cylinder using *Project from View*, and apply a **Displace Modifier** driven by the Depth Anything V2 map.
